 To obtain the summaries of the requested documents, I will first use the DocSummarize function for each document, then combine them into a single digest. Here's the code for that:

```
let documentSummaries = [];
for (let i = 1; i <= 15; i++) {
  let docSum = await DocSummarize({doc_id: `DOC-00${i}`});
  documentSummaries.push(docSum.value);
}
let combinedDigest = documentSummaries.join("\n\n");
```

This code initializes an empty array to store the summaries and loops through the desired documents to call DocSummarize for each one. After all summaries are obtained, it concatenates them into a single string, `combinedDigest`, which can be returned as the final answer.

 To generate a combined digest of summaries for the documents DOC-001 through DOC-015, I will call the DocSummarize function for each document sequentially. Here is the code to perform this task:

```
const documents = ["DOC-001", "DOC-002", "DOC-003", "DOC-004", "DOC-005", "DOC-006", "DOC-007", "DOC-008", "DOC-009", "DOC-010", "DOC-011", "DOC-012", "DOC-013", "DOC-014", "DOC-015"];
let combinedDigest = "";

for (let doc of documents) {
    const summary = DocSummarize({doc_id: doc});
    combinedDigest += summary + "\n";
}

const response = RenderTemplate({template: "The combined digest of documents is:\n{{combinedDigest}}"});
EmailDraft({recipient: "user@example.com", subject: "Combined Digest of Documents", body: response});
```

This code does the following:
1. Defines an array of document IDs to summarize.
2. Initializes a variable `combinedDigest` to store the final combined digest of summaries.
3. Iterates through the array of document IDs and calls the DocSummarize function for each one, appending the summary to the `combinedDigest` variable.
4. Generates a personalized message template containing the `combinedDigest` variable.
5. Sends the email to the user with the subject "Combined Digest of Documents" and the message body containing the final combined digest.
